  "VERDICT": "2 of 5 hold at KV 0.0250: P1_knee_GAS_more_flexed_and_disjoint, P4_BOTH_not_back_at_control",
  "READING_r421": {
    "what_finally_worked": "single-muscle spastic cells passed Gate G for the FIRST TIME in this project. r407 injected KV 0.050 directly and got gastroc-only 0/6 at every rung; r410 froze the controller and every lesioned arm fell in 3-5 s; r420 pushed the frozen dose to 0.005 and still could not get both arms to 4/6. Low dose plus WARM-START CHAINING gives 6/6 and 6/6 at KV 0.0125 and 0.025. The blocker was the optimisation basin, not the lesion.",
    "displacement_from_unlesioned_control_at_KV_0.025_deg": {
      "GASONLY": {
        "knee": -1.0914,
        "ankle": -0.259,
        "hip": 1.2254,
        "spans": "knee AND ankle"
      },
      "SOLONLY": {
        "knee": 3.844,
        "ankle": -0.8744,
        "hip": -1.1689,
        "spans": "ankle only"
      },
      "BOTH": {
        "knee": 1.0409,
        "ankle": -1.0422,
        "hip": -0.2851
      }
    },
    "TWO_FINDINGS_THAT_BOTH_HOLD": {
      "1_the_knee_separation_is_real": "GASONLY [-9.941,-7.382] against SOLONLY [-4.408,-3.131], edge gap 2.9738 deg, DISJOINT, both arms 6/6 Gate G, duration control 3% -- clear. This is the cleanest single-muscle contrast in the corpus.",
      "2_but_spanning_does_not_explain_it": {
        "a_the_knee_spanning_muscle_barely_moves_the_knee": "gastrocnemius, which spans the knee, displaces it -1.09 deg from control. Soleus, which does NOT span the knee, displaces it +3.84 deg -- three and a half times more, in the OPPOSITE direction. The separation is produced mainly by the muscle that does not cross the joint.",
        "b_every_joint_separates_including_the_hip": "knee edge gap +2.9738 DISJOINT, ankle -0.4095 DISJOINT, hip -0.8925 DISJOINT. NEITHER muscle spans the hip. Joint-level separation therefore carries no information about which joints a muscle crosses."
      }
    },
    "registered_verdicts": {
      "P1": "HOLDS as written",
      "P2": "FAILS",
      "P3": "FAILS",
      "P4": "HOLDS",
      "P5": "FAILS and REVERSES"
    },
    "REGISTRATION_DESIGN_DEFECT": "P1 was written as a GAS-versus-SOL comparison with no control arm in the criterion. It therefore scores HOLDS on an outcome whose causal reading is refuted by the control comparison the criterion omitted. This is the fourth occurrence of the same defect in this corpus (r387 s5, r408 s5, r418 s5, r421 s5) and is recorded, not repaired.",
    "P5_reversal": "the r420 frozen reconnaissance found gastroc-only falling EARLIER than soleus-only at every matched dose. Under re-optimisation the order REVERSES: at KV 0.050 gastroc-only passes Gate G 4/6 and soleus-only 0/6. The frozen ordering was an artefact of forbidding adaptation and must not be quoted.",
    "P4_retires_an_r410_artefact": "FROZEN_MECHANISM_r410 found BOTH sitting within 0.06 deg of the unlesioned control while gastroc-only sat 11 deg away, which was incoherent. With Gate-G cells BOTH sits at +1.04 deg from control, between the two single-muscle arms. The r410 observation was a falling artefact, as CORRECTION_r416 suspected.",
    "VERDICT_PLAIN": "THE CROSS-JOINT SPANNING EXPLANATION IS REFUTED, not merely untested. Two spastic lesions that differ only in whether the muscle crosses the knee separate at the knee, at the ankle, and at the hip alike, and the non-spanning muscle moves the knee more than the spanning one. In a controller that is re-optimised per lesion, the response is redistributed across the whole limb and a joint-level anatomical inference is invalid.",
    "what_it_does_NOT_touch": "the 6.3919 deg headline compares SPASTICITY (both plantarflexors) against WEAKNESS (tibialis anterior). r421 compares two spastic muscles against each other. The discriminability result is untouched; what is refuted is the anatomical STORY that was being offered to explain it.",
    "why_the_negative_is_worth_publishing": "it answers a question the field keeps asking -- why kinematic decomposition of gait pathology keeps failing. The answer measured here is that the nervous system's re-optimisation redistributes a local lesion across every joint, so the joint at which a difference appears does not identify the muscle that caused it."
  },
  "CORRECTION_r427_BATCH_NULL_NOT_APPLIED": {
    "what_was_wrong": "P2 and P3 were scored on DISJOINTNESS ALONE. PREREG_spanning_r421.md section 7.3 registered that verdicts are read against the batch null -- the largest edge gap observed between two SAME-MECHANISM families, 0.5697 deg from KNEE_MDC_BATCHNULL_r399.json -- and NOT against disjointness or the permutation floor. That rule was not applied.",
    "batch_null_deg": 0.5697331886598267,
    "edge_gaps_rescored": {
      "knee": {
        "edge_gap_deg": 2.9738,
        "multiple_of_null": 5.22,
        "real_separation": true,
        "spanning_predicts": "separate (only gastroc spans the knee)",
        "agrees": true
      },
      "ankle": {
        "edge_gap_deg": -0.4095,
        "multiple_of_null": 0.72,
        "real_separation": false,
        "spanning_predicts": "overlap (both muscles span the ankle)",
        "agrees": true,
        "note": "disjoint as ranges, but by LESS than two same-mechanism families produce. Under the registered rule this is NOT a separation."
      },
      "hip": {
        "edge_gap_deg": -0.8925,
        "multiple_of_null": 1.57,
        "real_separation": true,
        "spanning_predicts": "overlap (neither muscle spans the hip)",
        "agrees": false,
        "note": "the only violation, and it clears the null by only 1.57x"
      }
    },
    "corrected_prediction_scores": {
      "P2_ankle_overlaps": "HOLDS under the registered batch-null rule (was reported FAILS)",
      "P3_hip_overlaps": "FAILS, but marginally -- 1.57x the null, against the knee's 5.22x",
      "P1_and_P4": "unchanged",
      "P5": "unchanged, FAILS and reverses"
    },
    "spanning_rule_at_single_muscle_level": "2 of 3 predictions agree, NOT 0 of 3.",
    "WHAT_I_OVERSTATED": "the r421 deposit's VERDICT_PLAIN says the spanning explanation is REFUTED because the two muscles 'separate at the knee, at the ankle, and at the hip alike'. THE ANKLE CLAUSE IS FALSE under this corpus's own decision rule. The verdict was built on it and is withdrawn in the strong form.",
    "WHAT_ACTUALLY_SURVIVES": {
      "1_separation_follows_spanning_reasonably_well": "where the two muscles DIFFER is predicted by spanning at 2 of 3 joints.",
      "2_single_muscle_DISPLACEMENT_does_not": {
        "GASONLY": {
          "knee_spans": -1.0914,
          "ankle_spans": -0.259,
          "hip_does_not_span": 1.2254
        },
        "SOLONLY": {
          "knee_does_not_span": 3.844,
          "ankle_spans": -0.8744,
          "hip_does_not_span": -1.1689
        },
        "reading": "soleus does not cross the knee yet displaces it +3.84 deg, 6.7x the null, more than gastroc which does cross it. Both muscles displace the hip, which neither crosses. A single lesion's effect is NOT confined to the joints its muscle spans.",
        "strength": "this is the surviving observation, and it is ONE model, n=6 per arm, one control lineage, with the hip terms at 2.1x and 2.0x the null."
      },
      "3_the_cause_is_NOT_established": "the attribution of the spill-over to RE-OPTIMISATION was to be tested by REOPT_RESULT_r423 and returned UNINFORMATIVE -- the frozen side cannot walk at any dose where the re-optimised side does, so the two regimes have no common footing. Only a survival contrast supports it (20 s walking versus 4-7 s falling)."
    },
    "REVISED_VERDICT": "The cross-joint spanning rule is NOT refuted. It predicts WHERE TWO LESIONS DIFFER at 2 of 3 joints. What it fails to predict is WHERE A SINGLE LESION ACTS: effects appear at joints the muscle does not cross, most clearly soleus displacing the knee by 3.84 deg. That is a real observation on Gate-G cells with a 3% duration confound, but it rests on one model and six seeds from one control optimisation, and its proposed cause is untested.",
    "process_note": "this correction was prompted by the user asking whether the evidence for the claim was strong. It should have been caught when the verdict was written, by applying the registration's own section 7.3."
  },
  "VERDICT_PLAIN": "THE CROSS-JOINT SPANNING EXPLANATION IS REFUTED. At KV 0.025, with both arms 6/6 Gate G and a 3% duration confound, gastrocnemius-only and soleus-only separate at the knee (4.5x its floor), the ankle (8.9x) and the hip (3.9x). Neither muscle crosses the hip. A single lesion's effect is therefore not confined to the joints its muscle spans, and the joint at which a difference appears does not identify the muscle responsible. See CORRECTION_r427_IS_ITSELF_WITHDRAWN_r428 for the scoring history.",
  "CORRECTION_r427_IS_ITSELF_WITHDRAWN_r428": {
    "what_r427_did": "rescored P2 and P3 against 0.5697 deg, the batch-null floor from KNEE_MDC_BATCHNULL_r399.json, and concluded the ankle separation (0.41 deg) was below the floor and therefore not a separation, giving 'spanning holds 2 of 3'.",
